SSEECCUURRIITTYY
     Access to the llooaaddeerr__44tthh command line provides several ways of compromis‐
     ing system security, including, but not limited to:

     ••   Booting from removable storage, by setting the _c_u_r_r_d_e_v or _l_o_a_d_d_e_v
         variables

     ••   Executing binary of choice, by setting the _i_n_i_t___p_a_t_h or _i_n_i_t___s_c_r_i_p_t
         variables

     ••   Overriding ACPI DSDT to inject arbitrary code into the ACPI subsystem

     One can prevent unauthorized access to the llooaaddeerr__44tthh command line by
     setting the _p_a_s_s_w_o_r_d, or setting _a_u_t_o_b_o_o_t___d_e_l_a_y to -1.  See
     loader.conf(5) for details.  In order for this to be effective, one
     should also configure the firmware (BIOS or UEFI) to prevent booting from
     unauthorized devices.

